INSTRUCTIONS

Welcome to the Athletics Race Simulator. This program allows you to simulate a race between multiple participants using performance metrics that influence how each athlete runs the race.

SETUP PROCESS

Enter the race distance in metres when prompted.

Enter the number of participants who will compete in the race.

Enter how much you would like the race simulation to be sped up (for example, entering 5 will run the simulation at 5× normal speed).

After these values are entered, you will be asked to provide information for each participant.

PARTICIPANT METRICS

Each participant requires a name, a personal best time, and one or more performance ratings depending on the race distance.

Start Score (100m races only)

A rating from 1 to 10 that represents how strong the participant’s sprint start is.

Athletes with a higher start score accelerate more quickly out of the blocks.

This metric only appears when the race distance is 100 metres.

Kick Score

A rating from 1 to 10 that represents how strong the participant’s finishing sprint is.

Athletes with higher kick scores will accelerate more during the final portion of the race.

Experience Score

A rating from 1 to 10 representing the participant’s experience in the event.

Participants with low experience scores are more likely to start the race too quickly and slow down later.

Participants with high experience scores tend to pace themselves more evenly throughout the race.

TIME FORMAT

All participant times must follow a specific format and must be recorded to two decimal places.

Examples:

Middle or long distance: 5:30.00 (minutes.milliseconds)

Sprint events: 10.25 (seconds.milliseconds)

GENERAL RULES

All scores must be integers between 1 and 10.

Times must always include two decimal places.

Every participant must have all required fields completed before the race can begin.

Once all participants have been entered successfully, the race simulation will begin.